Package: academiccareer
Title: Descriptive, Evidence-Based Profiles of Academic Careers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Describes how a research career develops over time across the
    dimensions that responsible research assessment asks to recognise, not
    only publications: research outputs, software, data, funding, positions,
    supervision and teaching, peer review and service, knowledge transfer,
    science policy and open science. Evidence is collected from the public
    records of 'ORCID' <https://orcid.org/>, 'OpenAlex' <https://openalex.org/>
    and 'DataCite' <https://datacite.org/>, completed with evidence declared by
    the researcher, and placed in context, including career breaks. The
    package builds timelines, contributions by period, rule-based career
    transitions and a descriptive profile that highlights contributions such
    as software, data, transfer or teaching, with the coverage of each source
    stated explicitly. It does not rank or score researchers, does not compare
    people, and does not use journal-based metrics.
